From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tinycast Recipe <recipe@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:45:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] tinycast-space 0011: raycast themes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Raycast themes, as Raycast does them. Settings → General → Appearance has a *Light theme* and a *Dark theme* slot; the appearance Tinycast draws in (System follows macOS) picks between them. Each slot opens a browser of that appearance's themes — ray.so's catalog (`RaycastThemeCatalog.swift`, generated by `tools/raycast-themes.py`, MIT notice included) plus imported ones — under a live preview of the hovered theme. A *Theme* command lists the installed themes and previews each one on the window as it is highlighted: it is a small extension Tinycast writes into its own extensions folder at launch (`RaycastThemeCommand.swift`, fed `assets/themes.json`), so no palette mode or command enum changes. A theme swaps hues, never alphas: the ink ramp takes its `text`, the selection fill its `selection`, the palette's backdrop Raycast's gradient from `background` to `backgroundSecondary` (70 % down, as ray.so draws it; *Theme background*, `spaceRaycastThemeBackgroundOpacity`, default 70 %), floating glass (menus, the action capsule) a tint of `background`, other surfaces' scrim `background`, and extension `Color.Red` and friends its named colors. Tokens read an observable revision as they are drawn, so a theme change redraws exactly the views showing a themed color, in place and without an appearance flash. A `raycast://theme` link — outside, *Import Link from Clipboard*, or an extension's `open()` — asks in a dialog (Use Theme / Just Add / Cancel) over the palette, and the `closeMainWindow` Raycast Explorer sends right after is skipped; the Theme command's own links carry `apply=1` and switch at once. While an extension row whose `Action.Open` targets a theme link is highlighted, the palette alone shows that theme (the runtime now passes `Action.Open`'s `target` as a prop). The core (`RaycastThemeCore.swift`) is AppKit/SwiftUI-only because `Theme.swift` reads it and harnesses compile `Theme.swift` alone. The extension bridge also hands `raycast://confetti` to patch 0007 now — an extension's confetti link used to just reopen the launcher. Upstream declined themes (abue-ammar/tinycast#640).

Origin: tinycast-space 0011-raycast-themes.patch @ ffccfc3
